# Tracer: honest partial To-Lean compilation
#
# Before (did not work):
# 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 = 1 / 24
# sin(0) = 0
# 1 / 3 + 2 / 3 = 1
# Former behavior: strict To-Lean stopped at sin(0) = 0 and returned no Lean source.
#
# Now (verified):
1 / 2 / 3 / 4 = 1 / 24
sin(0) = 0
1 / 3 + 2 / 3 = 1
# Current behavior: report mode returns Incomplete, identifies statement 2, and emits
# checked Lean declarations for statements 1 and 3 with no axiom or sorry fallback.
#
# Boundary: parse errors and unverified Litex statements remain hard errors; strict
# To-Lean remains fail-closed for callers that require an all-or-nothing conversion.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/to_lean_partial_report.lit
# Focused compiler gate: cargo test --release to_lean_partial_report -- --nocapture
# Implementation: src/to_lean/compilation_report.rs and src/to_lean/to_lean_pipeline.rs
